    <string name="hands_note_1">The best five cards count, out of your two and the five shared.</string>
    <string name="hands_note_2">With the same hand the higher one wins: first the pair, the three or the straight, then card by card the rest.</string>
    <string name="hands_note_3">In a full house the three decide: 8-8-8-K-K beats 7-7-7-A-A.</string>
    <string name="hands_note_4">The ace is the highest card, but it also starts the lowest straight: A-2-3-4-5. A straight does not wrap: Q-K-A-2-3 is not one.</string>
    <string name="hands_note_5">Suits have no order: two equal hands split the pot.</string>
